---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const faqs = [
	{
		q: "Is LanternCert completely free?",
		a: `Yes! <strong class="text-key">Every overview, guide, and practice question is free</strong>. There is no paid tier waiting behind the free one.`,
	},
	{
		q: "Do I need to sign up for anything?",
		a: `No. <strong class="text-key">You do not need an account to use any feature</strong>. Some features, like storing and viewing your previous Mock Test scores, do require localStorage enabled on your device.`,
	},
	{
		q: "Where does your info come from?",
		a: `<strong class="text-key">From the official agencies that authorize and oversee certifications</strong>. This typically means your state's government, authorized third parties, and their publications and statutes. Every fact and question answer links to the document backing it up.`,
	},
	{
		q: "How do I know your info is current?",
		a: `<strong class="text-key">State-specific certification pages each show the date their facts were last validated</strong> against their sources. We automatically check to see when a source gets updated, then personally review what's changed.`,
	},
	{
		q: "Are the practice questions real exam questions?",
		a: `No. <strong class="text-key">No legitimate prep site has the real question bank</strong>. Ours are written fresh from each state's own material to cover the same ground the real exam covers. If an official practice test does exist, we ensure we link to it in addition to providing our own.`,
	},
];
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="What LanternCert is, how our study material is sourced and kept current, and how we handle your data."
>
	<div class="stack-lg col-center">
		<div class="stack">
			<h1 class="page-title">About LanternCert</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				LanternCert puts together need-to-know certification info in a single place. 
        All of our facts and study materials originate from, cite,
				and link to primary sources published by topical authorities.
			</p>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					LanternCert's mission is to validate and simplify every certification process in every
					state, one at a time. All without any ads, paywalls, or required signups, so you can focus
					on what matters most: getting certified.
				</p>
				<p>
					Preparing for a certification can sometimes be done with a few quick searches, and other
					times requires purchasing an expensive course; LanternCert exists to fill the gap. The idea
					was inspired by my time working in the education sector, as well as my frustration with
					learning about how to get (and later transfer) my motorcycle endorsement. I felt I could
					make something more helpful and beginner-friendly than what was out there, so I did.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<section class="stack framed" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
			<h2 class="section-title" id="faq-heading">Important questions / FAQ</h2>
			<ul class="faq">
				{
					faqs.map((faq) => (
						<li>
							<details class="faq__item">
								<summary>{faq.q}</summary>
								{/* set:html because an answer is authored copy carrying its own markup. */}
								<p set:html={faq.a} />
							</details>
						</li>
					))
				}
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="stack" aria-labelledby="privacy-heading" id="privacy">
			<h2 class="section-title" id="privacy-heading">Privacy and usage</h2>
			<div class="prose prose--sm">
				<p>
					<strong class="text-key">
						We do not ask for, collect, or store your name, email, or any other personal information.
					</strong>
				</p>
				<p>
					Anything you do on this site that is recorded specific to you, including your test results
					and preferences, is saved only on the device and browser you are using, is never sent to
					us, and is never sold or shared with anyone. You can download, opt out of, or erase this
					data yourself at any time from your <a href="/progress">progress page</a>, and clearing
					your browser data will immediately and permanently remove any locally tracked data as well.
				</p>
				<p>
					Google Analytics is used sitewide to collect aggregate usage statistics, such as which
					pages and questions get used and how, which helps to determine what is and isn't working.
					That measurement is anonymous and is never tied to any individual person.
				</p>
				<p>
					Pages with a state selector guess your state so the field is more likely to start on the right
					one. That guess is provided to LanternCert from Cloudflare, which hosts this site and can
					see roughly where a connection comes from based on the requestor's IP address. LanternCert
					never reads, stores, or is passed your IP address.
				</p>
				<p>
					By using this site, you acknowledge that LanternCert is free certification and exam prep
					material, not legal advice. Always confirm requirements with your state's official
					certification agencies or authorized third parties (which we cite; click the links!).
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
</Layout>
